      "explain": "<strong>Stage fear</strong> (also called speech anxiety or glossophobia) is the body's normal stress response to being watched. Your body releases adrenaline, which raises your heartbeat and breathing. The goal is not to eliminate it but to <strong>channel it into energy</strong>.",
