      "examAnswer": "Stage fear, also known as speech anxiety, is the anxiety experienced by a speaker before or during a presentation before an audience. It is a natural physiological response in which the release of adrenaline increases the heart rate and breathing and causes symptoms such as dryness of the mouth, trembling hands and a shaking voice. It can be managed through thorough preparation and repeated rehearsal, particularly of the opening of the speech, deep and slow breathing before speaking, early arrival to become familiar with the venue and equipment, positive self-talk, establishing eye contact with receptive members of the audience, deliberate use of pauses instead of hurrying, and concentrating on the message and the benefit to the audience rather than on oneself. With regular practice, the level of anxiety reduces considerably.",
